From 626569961e47c1ee6127652e4ba83f4e863aa952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:28:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop stripe red-reason: keep turn-live prompts,
 re-report a moved prompt, "as of" wording

Follow-up to 53638e3f239 (PR #1878), non-blocking nits from review t_01a1d340c6c3e24e (t_01a1d3474919d690).

1. supersededPromptRuntimes retired a sibling {needsInput, turnLive, !busy}, contrary to its docstring ("only a
   sibling no longer running is retired"). It now also skips turnLive siblings, like busy/awaitingResponse ones.
2. The sidebar effect that records/reports a row's stripe depended only on [session, statusStripe, dotState], but
   a needs-input row's reasons read $sessionStates / $pausedQueueSessionIds. When the prompt moved to another
   runtime the stripe and dot stayed the same, so the new red was never re-reported. New computed string store
   $stuckPromptInputsKey (needs-input runtimes with their stored ids + paused-queue ids) is now an effect
   dependency; being a string, rows re-render only when that set changes, not on every session-state publish.
3. describe() printed "Desktop stripe <x> since <at>", but `at` is the latest report time (a red edge, a cause
   change or a first sighting after a restart): now "as of".

Proof: new tests in session-states-stale-prompt.test.ts ("leaves a sibling whose turn is live...") and
session-row-stripe.test.tsx ("a red row whose prompt moved to another runtime is re-reported...") each fail with
their fix reverted (2 failed / 12) and pass with it; vitest src/store + src/app/chat/sidebar green; tsc -p . clean;
eslint clean; tests/hermes_cli/test_session_outcome_surfaces.py passes.
